{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "tone-generated-api-keys-2026-07-24",
    "name": "Generated API Keys API",
    "description": "Auto-generated from `core/api/v1/generated_api_keys.py` (mirrored by `ee/api/v1/generated_api_keys.py` — same paths, EE swaps the auth guards).\n\n**Prefix**: `/api/v1/generated-api-keys`\n\n**What this controller owns**\nCustomer-facing programmatic-access API keys. Distinct from `api_keys` (Model Providers) — those are provider credentials for LLM/STT/TTS services. A row here represents one Bearer token a customer sends in `Authorization: Bearer tone_sk_...` to hit the Tone API on behalf of their org.\n\n**Security model**\n- Full key format: `tone_sk_<32-char base62>`. Returned **exactly once** on create (in the `key` field of the response). After that the plaintext is unrecoverable — only `key_prefix` (~12 chars) is retained for display.\n- Server stores only SHA-256(`full_key`). A DB dump does NOT leak usable keys.\n- Every API-key-authenticated request runs at **admin** authority within the key's org (mirrors OpenAI / Retell / Stripe).\n- EE guard also blocks the `tenant_id` header switch for API-key callers so a key can never reach across into another org.\n\n**Auth matrix**\n| Endpoint | Core | EE |\n|---|---|---|\n| `create_api_key`  | `require_admin_or_owner` | `require_ee_admin_or_owner` |\n| `list`            | `require_org_member`     | `require_ee_org_member`     |\n| `get_api_key`     | `require_org_member`     | `require_ee_org_member`     |\n| `revoke_api_key`  | `require_admin_or_owner` | `require_ee_admin_or_owner` |\n| `delete_api_key`  | `require_admin_or_owner` | `require_ee_admin_or_owner` |",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
